{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI"]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/active","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/background","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/inactive"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","anchor":"Default-Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/Comparable-Implementations","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"text":"An indication of a scene’s operational state.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s15BitwiseCopyableP","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SL","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SQ","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/SH","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScenePhase","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The system moves your app’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instances through phases that reflect"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a scene’s operational state. You can trigger actions when the phase changes."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Read the current phase by observing the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/scenePhase","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value in the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"How you interpret the value depends on where it’s read from."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"If you read the phase from inside a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instance, you obtain a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that reflects the phase of the scene that contains the view. The following"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example uses the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/View\/onChange(of:perform:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method to enable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a timer whenever the enclosing scene enters the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/active","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" phase"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and disable the timer when entering any other phase:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MyView: View {","    @ObservedObject var model: DataModel","    @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase","","    var body: some View {","        TimerView()","            .onChange(of: scenePhase) { phase in","                model.isTimerRunning = (phase == .active)","            }","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you read the phase from within an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/App","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instance, you obtain an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"aggregate value that reflects the phases of all the scenes in your app. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"app reports a value of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/active","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if any scene is active, or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value of "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/inactive","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" when no scenes are active. This includes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"multiple scene instances created from a single scene declaration; for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, from a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". When an app enters the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/background","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" phase, expect the app to terminate soon after."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can use that opportunity to free any resources:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            MyRootView()","        }","        .onChange(of: scenePhase) { phase in","            if phase == .background {","                \/\/ Perform cleanup when all scenes within","                \/\/ MyApp go to the background.","            }","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you read the phase from within a custom "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instance, the value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"similarly reflects an aggregation of all the scenes that make up the custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scene:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct MyScene: Scene {","    @Environment(\\.scenePhase) private var scenePhase","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            MyRootView()","        }","        .onChange(of: scenePhase) { phase in","            if phase == .background {","                \/\/ Perform cleanup when all scenes within","                \/\/ MyScene go to the background.","            }","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenephase"]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"enum","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScenePhase","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"ScenePhase","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI10ScenePhaseO","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScenePhase","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration"},"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/App":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"App","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"App","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/app","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/App","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that represents the structure and behavior of an app."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"App","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ScenePhase":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScenePhase","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An indication of a scene’s operational state."}],"title":"ScenePhase","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScenePhase","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenephase"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Environment":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Environment","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environment","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A property wrapper that reads a value from a view’s environment."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ScenePhase/Comparable-Implementations":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/Comparable-Implementations","role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[],"title":"Comparable Implementations","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenephase\/comparable-implementations"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/ScenePhase/active":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/ScenePhase\/active","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The scene is in the foreground and interactive."}],"title":"ScenePhase.active","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"active","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/scenephase\/active"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/scenePhase":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwift